{%- comment -%}
  The one "is this a memory-foam bed?" test, shared by everything that makes
  a foam-specific claim about a product: the foam guarantee line and
  per-night price (buy box, cards, finder result via Lunova.foamBed), the
  cost reframe, the mechanism diagram and the comparison table.

  A product passes when its title, type or tags mention orthopaedic /
  orthopedic / memory foam. Merchants override it per product with ONE tag
  pair: "guarantee:yes" (treat as a foam bed the guarantee covers) or
  "guarantee:no" (never). guarantee:no wins over guarantee:yes.

  Output: the word "true" for a foam bed, nothing otherwise. Capture it:
    {%- capture is_foam -%}{%- render 'foam-bed', product: product -%}{%- endcapture -%}
    {%- if is_foam == 'true' -%} … {%- endif -%}

  Keep in step with Lunova.foamBed() in assets/global.js.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  if product != blank
    assign fb_tags = product.tags | join: ',' | downcase | prepend: ',' | append: ','
    assign fb_hay = product.title | append: ' ' | append: product.type | append: ' ' | append: fb_tags | downcase
    assign fb_ok = false
    if fb_hay contains 'orthopaedic' or fb_hay contains 'orthopedic' or fb_hay contains 'memory foam' or fb_hay contains 'memory-foam'
      assign fb_ok = true
    endif
    if fb_tags contains ',guarantee:yes,'
      assign fb_ok = true
    endif
    if fb_tags contains ',guarantee:no,'
      assign fb_ok = false
    endif
    if fb_ok
      echo 'true'
    endif
  endif
-%}
